                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7bbb78c6-2b4f-3abb-8522-c647f2db9131",
                        "entry_id": "2bd7e510-c653-3131-8171-cb8d1bfb45a2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To convert (iron) into steel, or to coat with a layer of steel by converting only the surface of the iron."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "976739fd-75a5-4e79-9564-89d107c2c4a9",
                                "sense_id": "7bbb78c6-2b4f-3abb-8522-c647f2db9131",
                                "text": "The success of an attempt to acierate iron will depend on the amount of nitrogen contained by the iron during carburation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "09369266-4bc5-44cc-a215-e8c0f4777285",
                                "sense_id": "7bbb78c6-2b4f-3abb-8522-c647f2db9131",
                                "text": "As an economy measure, the manufacturer decided to use iron rather than steel, but to acierate the surface to limit oxidation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "943b02be-2bde-4392-9145-23c63507904c",
                                "sense_id": "7bbb78c6-2b4f-3abb-8522-c647f2db9131",
                                "text": "The effect of manganese, whose influence on acieration is known to all manufacturers, is probably due to its rapid oxidation, thus producing a metallic oxide capable of completing the fining of the iron, and this, by eliminating any foreign body, facilitates the acierating process."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "abb21f04-2aef-4880-9850-e569042cb293",
                                "sense_id": "7bbb78c6-2b4f-3abb-8522-c647f2db9131",
                                "text": "It was noted by Biringuccio in 1540, and described by Agricola in \"De Re Metallica\" 1561 — that a bar of wrought iron, kept immersed long in molten cast iron, became acierated by taking up the carbon of the cast iron."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6f05d211-7412-4130-ab5f-862b3e1cf1fd",
                                "sense_id": "7bbb78c6-2b4f-3abb-8522-c647f2db9131",
                                "text": "Activities: Production of stone crushers (capacity from 0.3 to 2.5 metric tonnes a batch), blasting machines (compression capacity of 160 tonnes), and steel-acierating machines."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
